  "reason": "ASC 470-10-45-10 requires reclassification of long-term debt to current if a covenant breach exists and the lender can demand repayment. The waiver is only for six months, which is less than the typical operating cycle. The breach persists beyond the waiver period, so the debt should be classified as current. The statement incorrectly classifies $17,296 million as non-current."
